+/**
+ * The `HEAD` of the repository containing the project at the moment this
+ * revision was written, and whether that tree was clean.
+ *
+ * Read the name literally: this is the head observed at journal-write time, not
+ * the child's execution baseline. For a host that returns after the child
+ * finishes, the acceptance revision is written after the child's last task
+ * commit, so `sha` will normally be that commit rather than the phase base. The
+ * two coincide only for a revision written before launch. What the slot makes
+ * auditable is the journal-write ordering itself: a revision whose `sha` equals
+ * the recorded phase base proves the write did not precede baseline capture, and
+ * a revision whose `sha` descends from it proves the child ran first.
